# Customer Website Runtime Delivery V1

Migration: `supabase/migrations/20261935800000_customer_website_runtime_delivery_v1.sql`  
Library: `lib/customer-website-runtime/`  
API: `/api/runtime/v1/website/*`  
Feature owner: **PLATFORM** (control plane) + **APP** (readiness) + **customer runtime** (render/ack)

## Authoritative chain

Platform → APP → canonical delivery → installation/installId → customer runtime → acknowledgement → HTTP read-back → checksum → status.

## Rules

1. **No customer-specific Core code** — never hardcode domain, customer, organization, website, or install identifiers (including real customer hostnames).
2. **No pilot bypass** — ordinary customers use the same contract; no alternate delivery model.
3. **No direct DB from customer runtime** — only installation-token RPCs via Aipify server routes.
4. **Server-resolved only** — customer/org/website/domain/installation/version are never selected by query/body/header from the client.
5. **Installation token server-side only** — never log, never return, never put in public docs as a live secret.
6. **Default deny routes** — only explicitly mounted paths are served; homepage is disabled by default.
7. **Safe fallback** — on timeout, network failure, invalid payload, checksum mismatch, or unpublished website, fall back to the customer's own runtime.
8. **Full green requires three proofs** — DB checksum match + installation acknowledgement + HTTP read-back with proof headers. Never mark `active` from DB resolve alone (`pending_runtime` until ack + HTTP).
9. **HTTP verifier SSRF protection** — verified host only, DNS private-IP block, manual redirects same-host only, timeout, body-size limit; `200` without proof headers is rejected.
10. **Rollback history preserved** — never delete versions/revisions/operations; rollback follows the same pending_runtime → ack → HTTP chain.
11. **No false active** — client cannot submit verified status; server computes acknowledgement/HTTP status.
12. **Migration apply-side effects = 0** — no customer/website/page/version seeds, no HTTP, no auth/email/payment/DNS.
13. **Staging V2 stays separate** — path-based staging on APP host must not be broken; ordinary Production status distinguishes DB / ack / HTTP / fully verified.
14. **Canonical delivery reused** — extend delivery metadata; do not create a parallel entitlement or CMS model.
15. **Domain ownership** — Aipify Group AS does **not** own `aipify.com`. That domain is forbidden for Production data, generated emails, internal/staging identities, defaults, fixtures, migrations, and documentation examples that can be copied into Production. Only verified/owned Aipify domains (primary: `aipify.ai`) may be used for Aipify identities. Example code must use reserved example domains (`customer.example`, `example.com`) or an explicitly owned Aipify domain. Negative tests that reject `aipify.com` are allowed. Production release **stops** if an unauthorized Aipify domain appears in the active feature diff or generative path. Policy: `lib/aipify-domain-ownership/`.

## Proof headers

- `X-Aipify-Website-Version`
- `X-Aipify-Manifest-Checksum`
- `X-Aipify-Page-Checksum`
- `X-Aipify-Installation`

## Forbidden without a separate task

DNS · auth/password/MFA · payment/invoice · email · env/secrets rotation · dependency/lockfile changes · customer Production activation writes
